        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Most readers find 1b less clear than 1a. But they find 1c much less clear than either of the other two. The reason is this: in both 1a and 1b, the important characters (gold) are simple subjects (italicized) of verbs (bold). Even though 1b expresses important actions as abstractions (capitalized) rather than verbs, its subjects are still characters:",
